    "narrative": "The heart of today\u2019s lineup rests on the elite production expected from **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (80.53) and **Bryce Harper** (67.11). **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is our clear headliner; he faces a favorable matchup against Noah Schultz, and despite the \"Elite Hold\" risk associated with his stolen base upside, his placement in the #3 spot and a significant SP skill advantage make him our safest high-ceiling anchor. Similarly, **Bryce Harper** remains a must-start despite the 33% rain risk in his contest against Jos\u00e9 Soriano. His elite xwOBA of .388 provides a substantial floor that overrides the weather volatility, as we look to capitalize on his premium position in the order. **Jung Hoo Lee** also earns a strong recommendation (61.85) thanks to a favorable platoon split against Keider Montero, providing a reliable source of contact and run-scoring potential.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the final outfield spot, where **Gavin Sheets** (51.87) and **Tyler Freeman** (51.58) narrowly edged out **Dylan Beavers** (48.11). **Dylan Beavers** was the strongest bench candidate, but his projected matchup against Nathan Eovaldi\u2014a pitcher with an elite 3.36 xERA\u2014effectively capped his efficiency, causing the optimizer to favor the more favorable SP matchups presented to **Gavin Sheets** and **Tyler Freeman**. While **Cal Raleigh** (41.82) finds himself on the lower end of our starting efficiency spectrum due to a difficult matchup against the sharp Drew Rasmussen, he remains in the lineup to preserve positional depth and catch-volume for the week.\n\nInvestors should maintain high vigilance regarding the weather in the game featuring **Luis Arraez**, **Justin Crawford**, and **Bryce Harper**, as the 33% rain risk could compress the effective game time for three of our primary contributors. Furthermore, with the majority of the team currently in \"Lineup Pending\" status, the current scores are based on historical order 